The project is under MIT license, has 79 contributors, last release happened 3 weeks ago.

It is possible to use this library inside admin-panel.

Has support of multiple layouting libraries. Has a control panel and layout map component out of the box.

It is possible to define custom nodes with custom styling and react components inside, so it is pretty much possible to use it to update journey - action/state entities.

The node’s required fields are 

{noformat}type Node<Data> = {
  id: string;
  type: string;
  data: Data;
  position: {x: number; y: number};
}{noformat}

which gives a bit of inconvenience as we need to fill in positions of nodes beforehand, otherwise all the nodes will be drawn on top of each other

The edge’s required fields are

{noformat}type Edge = {
  id: string;
  source: string;
  target: string;
  sourceHandle: string;
}{noformat}

The {{ReactFlow}} component itself accepts {{onNodesChange}} and {{onEdgesChange}} callbacks, which makes it possible to create interactive graphs.

