Hi [~accountid:610a3ee66051c5006aeeeea1] , please find my replies in red below:


Current suggestions from the Estonian team include *delivering the parcel to the Bolt Office and asking the recipient to collect the parcel within 30 days*. +*In MT, it seems that this would require us getting a Postal Licence*+ (+we’ll have to check if it also needs to be registered in the commercial register+).

* _→_ [~accountid:6320602ec7601c8e4abeda47]{color:#4c9aff} {color}[~accountid:6273b7d8e51c620070bea596] {color:#4c9aff}_Please confirm if you would you be willing to do this in MT or if you envisage any other solution?_{color} 
{color:#bf2600}No, I would rule this out for 2 reasons: (1) We do not want to have a postal license, take on all the risks that come with it + take out an insurance policy & (2) When we move to new office premises, they are to remain on the down low and not openly known to the public for safety reasons. I think the solution should be much simpler: the fleet/driver would be providing a service under the postal license operator, therefore the driver can ‘hold onto the parcel’ until returned to the premises of the ‘fleet’. They are already responsible for the ‘safeguarding' of the object. If it needs to return to sender, then we can compensate the driver. This will be an iterative process, which we will learn from (i am expecting this scenario to be quite rare to be honest){color}

Currently *all drivers are automatically opted into this category* (as for all other categories). However, drivers can opt-out (the opt-in and opt-out flow of our current product only works one way, so you can either actively opt-in or opt-out and this is standardised for all categories). Due to this circumstance, *all high-risk markets affected by reclass are blocked for this project until the product is functional*. → [~accountid:6320602ec7601c8e4abeda47] [~accountid:6273b7d8e51c620070bea596] {color:#0747a6}Do you deem the risk okay in MT?{color} I’m asking as I don’t know well enough that market yet, however I seem to understand that the risk is mainly for couriers at the moment in MT… However, irrespective of the risks, I don’t think this would be possible in MT, considering that *in MT fleets need to obtain postal licence so really, only the ones which have obtained it should be able to opt in for that category, and before onboarding them we should check they have the necessary docs*

{color:#bf2600}No risk at all in my opinion. It would stand to reason that only drivers/fleets with the relevant legal documentation will be eligible to offer this service as a category choice. The above process you mentioned can be by-passed by first creating the car tags, then tagging only the vehicles belonging to the eligible fleets with the right documentation. Like that you won’t be mass-opting in.{color}

* Whether the rejection has an impact on the Driver Score or other matrices was *left to the local teams* by the global team. In any case, *delinking is possible*. → [~accountid:6320602ec7601c8e4abeda47] [~accountid:6273b7d8e51c620070bea596] {color:#4c9aff}_What would you like to go for in MT?_{color} In risky markets, we wouldn’t link rejection to Driver Score or any sanctions and perhaps there’s no point doing this at first in MT, considering the small numbers of fleets thta could perform that additional service?
{color:#bf2600}Agreed with you, no added value in linking them.{color}

